    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1954225327276007725",
      "url": "https://x.com/0xJiaming/status/1954225327276007725",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/0xJiaming/status/1954225327276007725",
      "text": "GN！\nImagine a global workshop that never closes—not in one city, but everywhere. A designer in Nairobi tags sensor data for autonomous drones. A lawyer in Madrid organizes legal case files. A gamer in Manila transcribes rare dialects. A robotics engineer in Tokyo refines perception systems for automation.\n\nThis isn’t science fiction—it’s the reality inside @JoinSapien . The platform brings together over one million contributors who have completed more than 80 million high-quality data tasks. Unlike traditional approaches that scrape the internet, Sapien sources highly specialized data directly from its global contributor network—mapping clinical reasoning in healthcare, annotating 3D sensor fusion data, transcribing multilingual audio, and more.\n\nThe biggest trust gap in AI comes from untrustworthy data. Misleading translations, misread traffic signs, fabricated citations—all trace back to the same root problem: noisy, unverified training data. Sapien addresses this from the ground up. Contributors stake tokens before starting tasks, every submission undergoes peer review, and only once it passes strict quality checks is payment in USDC released. Accuracy isn’t just encouraged—it’s built into the system.\n\nThe result is datasets enterprises can confidently deploy in critical systems, AI capable of reasoning in complex, high-stakes environments, and—perhaps most importantly—a future where we can trust AI because we trust the data it’s built on.",
      "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
